  "body": "Brand new and ready to move into, this five-bedroom home has the very latest in interior styling. It suits families who need space, flexibility and the best school zones on the Bays.\r\n\r\nTwo master suites, one on each floor\r\nThe ground-floor master has its own ensuite and wardrobe. It works well for extended family, guests, or anyone who would rather avoid the stairs. Upstairs, the second master is a private retreat. It has a walk-in wardrobe, an ensuite with a bath, and sliding doors that open onto a balcony with glass balustrades. Three more bedrooms upstairs all have built-in wardrobes and share a stylish family bathroom.\r\n\r\nA kitchen that stops you in your tracks\r\nCurves are the signature of this kitchen. Sculpted overhead cabinetry flows into a sweeping rounded island with a fluted base and curved stone edge tops. Brushed-brass fittings and light, modern tones keep it fresh and bright. Floor-to-ceiling handleless cabinetry hides a generous pantry and frames the integrated microwave and wall oven. A black glass induction cooktop sits beneath a picture window, and a lit display niche adds a touch of personality. Other details include:\r\n\r\n•A brushed-brass gooseneck mixer with a filtered water tap over a large undermount sink\r\n•Brass cabinet hardware\r\n•Warm LED strip lighting beneath the overheads and along the toe-kick\r\n\r\nEntertain in style\r\nBuilt-in cabinetry with a stone top runs along the dining area. It’s set up like a bar, ready for drinks, serving platters or a coffee station. From there, the living and dining area opens straight out to the lawn. The easy indoor-outdoor flow makes summer barbecues and keeping an eye on the kids effortless.\r\n\r\nQuality you can see in every detail\r\nThe finishing is what sets this home apart. It has designer light fittings, from sculptural wall sconces to a statement pendant over the dining table. The architraves and skirtings are high quality, the cornices are decorative, and picture-frame panelling with beautifully detailed mouldings runs through the dining area and hallway. The light-filled living area has wide-plank timber-look floors and floor-to-ceiling glazing on two sides. The bathrooms are finished to a boutique standard, with terrazzo floors, travertine-look tiles, a floating timber vanity, an arched brass mirror and a skylight.\r\n\r\nPremium outside too\r\nThe quality carries through to the exterior. Premium weatherboard and stacked stone cladding give the home real street presence. The landscaping is just as considered: a fully fenced lawn with a white picket fence, and a stepping-stone path set in bright white chip stones. It’s safe for kids and pets.\r\n\r\nBuilt for easy living\r\n\r\n•Heat pumps for year-round comfort\r\n•Keyless smart lock entry\r\n•Separate guest WC and laundry\r\n•Single garage with internal access\r\n•Low maintenance inside and out\r\n•10-year Stamford warranty\r\n\r\nLocation and schools\r\nThe home is in zone for Sherwood School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College, a sought-after combination for North Shore families. Westfield Albany, the Albany Park and Ride and SH1 are a short drive away. Browns Bay village and beach are about a kilometre from your door.\r\n\r\nYou won’t need to renovate, wait for a build or compromise. Just move in and enjoy.",
